# Rust
**/target/

# .NET
**/bin/
**/obj/
**/TestResults/
# The forge stages each RID's native library here at test and pack time (see
# hyper-build-native.yml and hyper-pack-nuget.yml); nothing under it is committed. Locally
# the csproj falls back to rust/target/release/ when this RID has nothing staged, so a
# plain `cargo cdylib` is all the dev loop needs.
csharp/HyperUuid/runtimes/
# The same for the static libraries a Native AOT publish links in: staged by the forge's
# static-libs/build-static-libs.sh at test and pack time, never committed.
csharp/HyperUuid/staticlibs/
# go/staticlib's archives ARE committed — a Go module is whatever is in the tree — but only
# by stage-native-binaries.yml, which adds them with `git add -f` after verifying each one's
# build provenance. Ignored here so that a developer's own build of them (the forge's
# static-libs/build-static-libs.sh, which `go test` needs to link) can never
# ride into a commit by accident.
go/staticlib/*/*.a

# Gradle / Java
**/.gradle/
**/build/
# Same story as csharp/HyperUuid/runtimes/ above: CI (the Forge's hyper-pack-maven.yml)
# bundles all platforms' natives here at pack time; regenerable locally via
# `cargo cdylib` for local dev/test.
java/src/main/resources/native/
# csharp/HyperUuid/build/ is NuGet's real, tracked build/{PackageId}.targets packaging
# convention (auto-imported into every consumer for the WASM NativeFileReference wiring — see
# HyperUuid.csproj), not a build output — collides with **/build/ above, which would otherwise
# silently swallow it. Each directory level needs its own negation; git won't descend into an
# excluded directory to find a deeper !file re-inclusion, and gitignore rules apply in file
# order, so this has to come after the rule it's un-ignoring.
!csharp/HyperUuid/build/
!csharp/HyperUuid/build/net10.0/
!csharp/HyperUuid/build/net10.0/HyperUuid.targets

# Python
**/__pycache__/
**/*.egg-info/
**/.venv/
**/dist/
**/.pytest_cache/

# Swift
# The core in the artifact bundle and the XCFramework is build output: CI and
# .github/scripts/local-core.sh write it, and consumers get it from the release's assets (the
# root Package.swift). Only the bundle's include/ (header and module map) is source.
**/.build/
swift/HyperUuidCore.artifactbundle/*
!swift/HyperUuidCore.artifactbundle/include/
swift/HyperUuidCoreApple.xcframework/

# Ruby
# Same story — CI places each leg's native lib here for `bundle exec rspec` at build-native
# time; regenerable locally via `cargo cdylib`.
ruby/lib/hyperuuid/native/*/
ruby/Gemfile.lock
ruby/pkg/
ruby/.yardoc/
# The wasm32-wasip1 archives `rake wasm:gem` packs (and their .gz), staged from CI's
# ruby-wasm-<minor> artifacts by release.yml, or by hand; never committed.
ruby/ext/hyperuuid_native/*/
# rbwasm's interpreter build and its output, from running ruby/wasm-smoke locally.
ruby/wasm-smoke/Gemfile.lock
ruby/wasm-smoke/build/
ruby/wasm-smoke/rubies/
ruby/wasm-smoke/*.wasm

# PHP
# Native libs under php/src/native/{rid}/ are committed, not ignored — see
# php/src/native/README.md for why (Packagist has no packing step, unlike every other
# registry this repo publishes to).
php/vendor/
php/composer.lock
php/.phpunit.result.cache
# Root-level composer.json exists only for Packagist (see php/README.md's Install section) —
# nothing actually runs `composer install` from the repo root except a consumer's own build,
# but a stray local one shouldn't get committed either.
/vendor/
/composer.lock

# Node: the TypeScript binding and ruby/wasm-smoke's test harness.
**/node_modules/
# The napi-rs addon `npm run build` writes for this machine, and the per-platform package
# directories `napi create-npm-dirs` writes (the Forge's pack-npm action runs it on a copy of
# typescript/ at release time); never committed.
typescript/*.node
typescript/npm/

# R. vendor.sh stages the core and the corpus, derives the wrapper crate's lock from
# rust/Cargo.lock and vendors the crates into these at release time, in CI and for the
# local loop; R CMD INSTALL leaves the objects and the library. All generated, never
# committed. r/.gitignore and typescript/.gitignore repeat their entries for their own trees.
r/src/rust/core/
r/src/rust/vendor/
r/src/rust/vendor.tar.xz
r/src/rust/Cargo.lock
r/src/.cargo/
r/tests/testthat/corpus/
r/src/*.o
r/src/*.so
r/src/*.dll

# BenchmarkDotNet
# Writes output relative to the process's working directory when invoked via `dotnet run`
# rather than the project directory, so this can land almost anywhere in the tree — not just
# csharp/HyperUuid.Benchmarks/. Criterion's own output already lands under rust/target/,
# covered by the **/target/ rule above.
**/BenchmarkDotNet.Artifacts/

# IDE
.idea/
.vs/
# Stale paths from before the maturin restructure (top-level sibling module, not nested) —
# harmless to keep matching in case any local checkout still has one lying around.
python/src/hyperuuid_native.so
python/src/hyperuuid_native.pyd
# The staged PyO3 extension for local dev/test — nested at hyperuuid._native (the maturin
# module-name), built from the core crate's python feature. maturin tags the file by ABI,
# Python version and platform (_native.abi3.so, _native.abi3t-darwin.so,
# _native.cpython-314t-<platform>.so and more), so these match every compiled spelling and
# nothing else: _native.pyi beside them is the tracked type stub.
python/src/hyperuuid/_native*.so
python/src/hyperuuid/_native*.pyd
# Staged Magnus extension for local dev/test (built from the core crate's `ruby` feature —
# `cargo ruby`; platform gems carry the real artifact).
ruby/lib/hyperuuid_native.so
ruby/lib/hyperuuid_native.bundle
# The per-ABI staging the fat platform gem is packed from (lib/hyperuuid/<minor>/), written
# by release.yml from CI artifacts. Same story as the flat pair above: build output, never
# committed. Scoped to the extension filename rather than the whole directory so it can't
# swallow a real lib/hyperuuid/*.rb source file if a minor-version-shaped one ever appears.
ruby/lib/hyperuuid/*/hyperuuid_native.so
ruby/lib/hyperuuid/*/hyperuuid_native.bundle

# The corpus copy test-apple-mobile stages for the Go suite in the iOS simulator
# (go_ios_exec carries only the module's testdata), if made by hand.
go/testdata/corpus/

# What Finder writes into any folder it opens.
.DS_Store
